Bootstrap from MSYS2 and Git Bash shells as from Cygwin.

bootstrap.sh switches its class path to Windows form only when uname says
CYGWIN. In MSYS2's and Git for Windows' shells it says MINGW64_NT or
MSYS_NT, so the relative, colon-separated class path reaches the Windows
javac unchanged and the bootstrap cannot compile. Both shells have cygpath,
which the Cygwin branch uses. The installed ant script already handles
these shells.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/bootstrap.sh
+++ b/bootstrap.sh
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 cygwin=false
 darwin=false
 case "`uname`" in
-  CYGWIN*)
+  CYGWIN*|MINGW*|MSYS*)
     cygwin=true
     ;;
   Darwin*)
